      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "4 BED SANCTUARY IN THE HEART OF THE CUILCAGH LAKELANDS GEOPARK WITH STUDIO AND EXTENSIVE OUTBUILDINGS ON 1.2 ACRES\n\nSome properties are measured by their square footage. Others are remembered for how they make you feel.\nPredominantly crafted in beautiful pine, the home exudes a timeless sense of comfort and character. Rich timber finishes, exposed beams and natural materials create a wonderfully welcoming atmosphere throughout, while large windows frame picturesque views of the surrounding gardens, ensuring the outdoors is never far from view.\n\nThe kitchen forms the true heart of the home, combining rustic charm with everyday practicality. Here, a solid fuel stove creates an inviting gathering place during the colder months, while the adjoining dining and living areas provide generous spaces for entertaining family and friends or simply enjoying peaceful evenings.\n\nExtending to approximately 2,092 sq.ft. the accommodation offers four generous bedrooms, multiple reception rooms, two bathrooms, a bright sunroom overlooking the gardens, spacious loft storage and flexible living spaces that can easily adapt to changing family needs. While beautifully maintained throughout, the property also offers exciting potential for modernisation, allowing the next owner to place their own stamp on an already exceptional home.\n\nOriginally centred around a charming cottage, this remarkable property has been lovingly transformed by its current owners since 1984 into an extraordinary countryside sanctuary. With thoughtful extensions, beautifully crafted interiors and gardens nurtured over four decades, it is a home where every tree, pathway and flowering border reflects a lifetime of passion, patience and respect for nature.\n\nDetached Studio with Approved Change of Use\n\n\nA valuable addition to the property is the detached 335 sq.ft. Studio, complete with a kitchenette, solid fuel stove, disabled access and accessible WC facilities, the building is ready to adapt to a variety of future uses.\n\nPlanning permission has been granted for its change of use to self-catering accommodation, with permission valid until March 2028. This presents an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking to establish a holiday let, guest accommodation or flexible ancillary living space in one of Ireland`s most scenic tourism destinations.\n\nOutside, the beautifully established grounds are home to over thirty species of native trees, complemented by magnificent conifers, umbrella pines, stone pines and an ever-changing display of seasonal planting. Carefully designed pathways meander through mature borders, hidden seating areas and tranquil corners where time seems to slow. An ornamental koi pond forms a peaceful focal point, while squirrels regularly visit the gardens and migrating birds arrive each autumn, drawn to the rich habitat that has been lovingly cultivated over the years. The owners have embraced an organic approach to gardening, allowing nature to flourish in harmony with the landscape and creating an environment that simply cannot be recreated overnight.\n\nAdding to the sense of escape are a greenhouse, sauna and a range of useful outbuildings, offering endless possibilities for gardening enthusiasts, hobbyists or those simply seeking a slower pace of life. Whether enjoying a morning coffee in the sunroom overlooking the gardens, tending to the greenhouse, foraging through the surrounding landscape or relaxing beneath the mature trees, every corner of the property invites you to reconnect with nature.\n\nFor the past twenty-five years, the owners have also operated an internationally recognised teddy bear-making business from the property, welcoming collectors and customers from around the world. Their passion for craftsmanship, heritage and creativity is reflected throughout the home, where carefully collected artefacts and personal touches create an atmosphere unlike anywhere else. Alongside this creative endeavour, the property has also hosted nature and heritage workshops, sharing the owners` lifelong appreciation of the surrounding landscape, wildlife and traditional skills.\n\nModern comforts blend seamlessly with its traditional charm. Solar panels, complete with battery storage and smartphone monitoring, provide excellent energy efficiency, with excess electricity exported back to the grid. During the summer months, the system is capable of heating the home`s water supply almost entirely. Flexible heating options include solar, oil-fired central heating and three solid fuel stoves, offering both efficiency and resilience. \n\nPerfectly positioned within the breathtaking Cuilcagh Lakelands Geopark, the property enjoys access to one of Ireland`s most spectacular natural playgrounds. Brackley Lough lies less than two minutes from the front door, offering opportunities for fishing, kayaking, paddleboarding and peaceful lakeside walks. The renowned Cuilcagh Boardwalk Trail, affectionately known as the Stairway to Heaven, together with the Marble Arch Caves, forest walks, scenic cycling routes and countless hidden beauty spots, are all within easy reach. It is a location that encourages an active outdoor lifestyle while offering the peace and privacy of rural living.\n\nDespite its wonderfully secluded setting, the property remains conveniently close to Bawnboy and Ballyconnell, where everyday amenities, schools, cafés and local services are readily available, providing the perfect balance of countryside tranquillity and modern convenience.\n\nProperties such as this rarely come to the market.This is far more than a house it is the culmination of forty years of vision, dedication and love for the natural world. It is a place where gardens have been patiently cultivated, wildlife has been encouraged to flourish, creativity has inspired visitors from across the globe, and every season brings new colour, new life and new memories.\n\nFor those seeking not simply a home, but a lifestyle defined by peace, privacy and a deep connection to nature, this remarkable property presents an opportunity that is truly one of a kind."
      },
      {
